  "id": "COMPOUND:15797 - PROTEIN:4978",
  "verbalization": "Coumanolignan is implicated in the interaction with C8166 through a series of molecular targets, primarily the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta. This enzyme is a common target of multiple compounds, including the coumanolignan itself, which is linked to the broader class of compounds known as Caryophylla-2(12),6-dien-5-one and Labradorin 1. These compounds are all known to interact with the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which in turn targets C8166. The evidence suggests that Coumanolignan may act through a shared mechanism involving the modulation of this ATPase, potentially by altering its activity or function. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta as a central mediator in the interaction between Coumanolignan and C8166, with the specific targeting of this enzyme providing a plausible mechanism for the observed relationship.",
